From: "John (PinKushin)" <pinkushin1@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 11:32:37 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] fix: HUD particle panels stay serial; test the
 duplicate-offer flush

A bare ParticleEffects now defaults to one worker, so only the scene's
instance follows cl_frame_workers and the HUD model panels stay serial as
the help text says. New test: a key offered twice in a frame gives the
frames of one offer; deleting the flush reddened it, restored.

Docs: finding 94 corrects its first bone-setup blocker (SkinnedModel's
caches are ConcurrentDictionary already), records that the seek-based shot
fallback also fails serial against serial, and qualifies the draw overlap's
3 ms as an estimate. The measurement's Result explains that the frame
column is not the phase sum, so its lower threaded reading is not a saving.

Tested by: ParticleEffectsWorkersTests (8), Scene.Tests 3220, Presentation.Tests 1274
Observed: docs/measurements/2026-10-22-threaded-particles.md

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
